WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.749
Welcome to Grade 6 English, Unit 5: Money Matters.

2
00:00:03.829 --> 00:00:11.101
Money is a part of everyday life, but understanding
how it works is a skill that takes practice.

3
00:00:11.181 --> 00:00:18.605
Whether you are saving coins in a jar at home,
choosing between two things you want at the market,

4
00:00:18.685 --> 00:00:24.349
or hearing adults talk about bills and
budgets, money is always around you.

5
00:00:24.429 --> 00:00:32.926
In this unit, you will explore the world of financial
literacy — the ability to understand and use money wisely.

6
00:00:33.006 --> 00:00:39.358
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

7
00:00:39.438 --> 00:00:47.675
By the end of this unit, you will be able to read and
understand texts about spending, saving, and financial literacy.

8
00:00:47.755 --> 00:00:52.750
You will also use comparative adverbs
correctly to compare actions (e.g.

9
00:00:52.830 --> 00:00:55.288
*more quickly*, *faster*, *better*).

10
00:00:55.368 --> 00:00:59.305
You will also use quantifiers to talk about amounts (e.g.

11
00:00:59.385 --> 00:01:02.618
*both*, *neither*, *some*, *many*, *a lot of*).

12
00:01:02.698 --> 00:01:05.226
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

13
00:01:05.306 --> 00:01:11.806
Your vocabulary work begins with these words: humble,
eagerly, meagre, firmly, sensitive, uncomfortable.

14
00:01:11.886 --> 00:01:16.931
Listen to each pronunciation in the
vocabulary lab, study its meaning in context,

15
00:01:17.011 --> 00:01:20.917
and use the word accurately in
your own discussion and writing.

16
00:01:20.997 --> 00:01:27.145
The reading sequence includes Money, Markets, and
Making Good Choices and A Conversation About Saving.

17
00:01:27.225 --> 00:01:28.000
Read actively.

18
00:01:28.080 --> 00:01:32.214
Identify each text's central ideas,
notice viewpoint and reliability,

19
00:01:32.294 --> 00:01:36.183
and support every inference with
relevant evidence from the text.

20
00:01:36.263 --> 00:01:39.480
The first language focus is Comparative Adverbs.

21
00:01:39.560 --> 00:01:43.602
Comparative adverbs let us compare how two actions are done,

22
00:01:43.682 --> 00:01:50.747
showing that one action happens in a greater or lesser
way than another, such as more quickly or faster.

23
00:01:50.827 --> 00:01:58.235
Notice the structure in the model examples, then apply
it deliberately in connected sentences and paragraphs.

24
00:01:58.315 --> 00:02:02.623
In speaking, you will complete
Speaking 1: Explain a Money Word.

25
00:02:02.703 --> 00:02:07.218
Organise your ideas, use evidence
and respond clearly to questions.

26
00:02:07.298 --> 00:02:10.715
In writing, you will plan, draft, check and revise.

27
00:02:10.795 --> 00:02:14.349
Use the success criteria before submitting your work.

28
00:02:14.429 --> 00:02:16.015
You are ready to begin.

29
00:02:16.095 --> 00:02:23.187
Start with the vocabulary lab, continue through
reading and comprehension, apply the grammar focus,

30
00:02:23.267 --> 00:02:26.664
and complete the speaking and writing practices.

31
00:02:26.744 --> 00:02:34.704
Use AI English for hints and feedback any time, and bring
your questions to a live session too if you join one.
